Cell["\<\
So we need take into account correcting conditions r \[LessEqual] s. More \
universal method however would be construct all outcomes and delete those \
output for which the condition don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t  hold.  This way we \
ensure that no other constrains exists for results which differ\
\>", "Text",
